description:
**What:** RFC 8620 §5.3 requires newState to reflect all mutations. Currently new_state is captured before the onSuccessSetIsDefault loop which calls update_object and mutates state.

**Algorithm:**
1. Set mutated = true inside the onSuccessSetIsDefault block when update_object succeeds.
2. Move the new_state fetch (currently before the onSuccessSetIsDefault block) to AFTER it:
   let new_state = if mutated {
       backend.get_state::<AddressBook>(&account_id).await.map_err(...)?
   } else {
       old_state.clone()
   };
3. Add test set_on_success_new_state_reflects_mutation: empty create/update/destroy, only onSuccessSetIsDefault triggers update; assert newState != oldState. Oracle: RFC 8620 §5.3.
4. cargo test -p jmap-contacts-server.

**Acceptance criteria:**
- newState reflects state after all mutations including post-set. Oracle: RFC 8620 §5.3.
- When no mutations: newState == oldState.
- cargo test exits 0.
